    <string name="monitor_examples_summary">What each setting is for</string>
    <string name="monitor_examples_hint">What each of these settings is for. This page only explains; it changes nothing for you — which app each one describes is something only you know.</string>
    <string name="monitor_example_own_use">A location app you open and use yourself</string>
    <string name="monitor_example_own_use_body">While it is open you already know it is using location. What you want told about is the rest of the time.

Suggested: off screen only · a minute or more · silent</string>
    <string name="monitor_example_quiet_location">An app you suspect of checking location quietly</string>
    <string name="monitor_example_quiet_location_body">You want to hear about every one, without it becoming a number that climbs while you are not looking.

Suggested: off screen only · every minute · pop up</string>
    <string name="monitor_example_sensors">The camera or microphone turning itself on</string>
    <string name="monitor_example_sensors_body">This should not be happening often, so nothing gets folded together and every one interrupts.

Suggested: off screen only · no limit · pop up</string>
    <string name="monitor_example_refusals">Checking that a permission you just denied is really blocked</string>
    <string name="monitor_example_refusals_body">Only the refusals answer that question; the accesses that went through are in the way.

Suggested: refused only · no limit · pop up</string>
    <string name="monitor_example_one_shot">Clipboard, contacts, messages, call log</string>
    <string name="monitor_example_one_shot_body">These are read one at a time and each read means something, so none should be missed. A read while you are watching counts too.

Suggested: no limit · leave off-screen-only off</string>
    <string name="monitor_example_unknown">Watching a permission for the first time</string>
    <string name="monitor_example_unknown_body">Some report far more often than you would expect. Start with an interval, watch it for a few days, and take it off once you know it is quiet.

Suggested: every 30 seconds · silent</string>
